{"id": "codec.saguaro_dynamic_range", "statement": "The saguaro fine band's cell-bundle |S| spans p99.9/p50 = {value}", "value": "28x", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/storage.md", "generator": "examples/run_codec_capture.py"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_codec_capture.py"], "patterns": ["dynamic range is (\\d+x) rather than"], "cites": ["docs/storage.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Was 987x pre-reach-split, which is why HM-4's max-scaling truncation was a stronger accidental denoiser then than now. The old value is quoted on the page under a historical marker."}
{"id": "coupling.gain_saguaro", "statement": "Orthogonal frequency coupling improves the saguaro slices by {value}", "value": "+18.4% / +17.6%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/spatial.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_coupling data/scan-tucson.spz"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_coupling.py", "holo/spectral.py"], "patterns": ["saguaro, 519k splats\\s+(\\+[\\d.]+% / \\+[\\d.]+%)"], "cites": ["docs/spatial.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Coupling is a variance reducer at fixed d and fixed bytes, so this is the share of saguaro's error that was Monte-Carlo variance. Compare coupling.gain_train."}
{"id": "coupling.gain_train", "statement": "Orthogonal coupling improves the dense train capture by only {value}", "value": "+1.9% / +1.5%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/spatial.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_coupling data/train.splat"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_coupling.py"], "patterns": ["train, 504k splats \\(dense\\)\\s+(\\+[\\d.]+% / \\+[\\d.]+%)"], "cites": ["docs/spatial.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "The key negative for issue #3: a variance reducer that removes 18% on saguaro removes ~nothing here, so the dense residual is not variance. Sharper than the d-doubling experiment and free."}
{"id": "denoise.gain_train", "statement": "Shrinkage at p25 improves the dense train capture by {value}", "value": "+40.1% / +19.4%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/spatial.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_coupling data/train.splat"}, "evidence": ["holo/denoise.py", "examples/run_coupling.py"], "patterns": ["train, 504k splats \\(dense\\)\\s+\\+[\\d.]+% / \\+[\\d.]+%\\s+(\\+[\\d.]+% / \\+[\\d.]+%)"], "cites": ["docs/spatial.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Far larger than shrinkage's 14.8%/4.8% on saguaro, and unchanged by coupling (40.5% after), so on dense scenes shrinkage removes error that is not variance."}
{"id": "project.window_whole_cell", "statement": "Windowed analytic projection decodes whole real cells at {value} relative error", "value": "0.0739", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_analytic_projection data/scan-tucson.spz"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_analytic_projection.py"], "patterns": ["Gaussian window, s = h/2\\s+0\\.\\d+\\s+(0\\.\\d+) \\(2\\.5x better\\)"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "tolerance": 0.005, "lane": "research", "notes": "Against forward encoding's 0.1879 on the same cells and points \u2014 2.5x better with zero samples. Median over the six most populated xfine cells of saguaro at d=2048."}
{"id": "project.box_interior", "statement": "The box objective reaches {value} on interior splats, where its right-hand side is valid", "value": "0.0273", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "INTERIOR=1 python -m examples.run_analytic_projection data/scan-tucson.spz"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_analytic_projection.py"], "patterns": ["box \\+ TSVD\\s+(0\\.\\d+) \\(5\\.4x better\\)"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "tolerance": 0.005, "lane": "research", "notes": "5.4x better than forward's 0.1464 on the same restricted cells. The box is the better OBJECTIVE and the unusable one: on whole cells it scores 0.2052, worse than forward, because its whole-space right-hand side is wrong for edge splats."}
{"id": "project.pipeline_saguaro", "statement": "Analytic projection decodes the saguaro slices at {value} end to end", "value": "0.2170 / 0.1367", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py"], "patterns": ["saguaro\\s+0\\.3501 / 0\\.2132\\s+(0\\.\\d+ / 0\\.\\d+)"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Against forward encoding's 0.3501/0.2132 on the same slices \u2014 +38.0%/+35.9%."}
{"id": "project.pipeline_train", "statement": "Analytic projection decodes the dense train slices at {value} end to end", "value": "0.3765 / 0.1716", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/train.splat"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py"], "patterns": ["train \\(dense\\)\\s+0\\.9591 / 0\\.4948\\s+(0\\.\\d+ / 0\\.\\d+)"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "+60.7%/+65.3% against forward. The largest of the three levers on the scene issue #3 is about, where coupling bought 1.9% and shrinkage 40.1%."}
{"id": "project.tikhonov_saguaro", "statement": "Tikhonov-regularised projection decodes saguaro at {value}", "value": "0.1227 / 0.0803", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz --tikhonov 1e-6"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py"], "patterns": ["1e-6\\s+(0\\.\\d+ / 0\\.\\d+) \\(\\+65"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "+65.0%/+62.3% against forward's 0.3501/0.2132, and better than the truncated solve's 0.2170/0.1367 at a quarter of the encode cost. lambda=1e-6 is the SPARSE setting; see project.tikhonov_lambda_regression."}
{"id": "project.tikhonov_lambda_regression", "statement": "The sparse lambda on the dense capture regresses to {value}", "value": "1.0351 / 0.3727", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/train.splat --tikhonov 1e-6"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py"], "patterns": ["1e-6\\s+0\\.\\d+ / 0\\.\\d+ \\(\\+65[^)]*\\)\\s+(1\\.\\d+ / 0\\.\\d+)"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "The failure mode: worse than forward encoding's 0.9591 on the top-down axis. The dense capture wants lambda=1e-1 or larger (0.2986/0.1388), five orders of magnitude away. Not a constant to inherit."}
{"id": "denoise.on_solved_bundle", "statement": "Shrinkage improves an already-solved saguaro bundle by {value}", "value": "+6.4% / +3.6%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz 0.25 --shrink"}, "evidence": ["holo/denoise.py", "examples/run_projection_pipeline.py"], "patterns": ["a further (\\+[\\d.]+% / \\+[\\d.]+%)"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Contradicts the prediction that a solved bundle leaves nothing to shrink: the solve is optimal for the windowed per-cell objective, not for the quantity being scored, and truncation means it is not optimal even for that."}
{"id": "codec.overwide_bits_corruption", "statement": "Before validation, a 17-bit polar code round-tripped at {value} relative \u2014 output unrelated to input", "value": "1.051", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/storage.md", "generator": "pack_polar/unpack round-trip on a 1024-component bundle at bits=17"}, "evidence": ["holo/phase.py", "tests/test_phase.py"], "patterns": ["17-bit round-tripped at ([\\d.]+) relative"], "cites": ["docs/storage.md"], "lane": "storage", "notes": "Silent-corruption regression pinned by tests/test_phase.py. Codes are stored as uint16 above 8 bits, so widths past 16 wrapped with no error and no warning; the decode side is checked too because `bits` is read from a header and is peer-controlled on a replicated blob."}
{"id": "sync.trim_full_d2048", "statement": "A 64-container replica after 30 edit rounds at d=2048 exports {value} MB as a full Snapshot", "value": 31.0, "units": "MB", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/sync.md", "generator": "HoloReplica.snapshot() vs .checkpoint() on a synthetic capture-shaped replica"}, "evidence": ["holo/crdt.py", "tests/test_crdt.py"], "patterns": ["30 edit rounds, d=2048\\s+([\\d.]+) MB"], "cites": ["docs/sync.md"], "lane": "sync", "notes": "The ratio is the edit-round count, not a codec-like constant: a trimmed doc costs its state, an untrimmed one costs its state once per round. An earlier note quoted '40x measured' from a 40-round replica and read it as a property of the format."}
