{"id": "sync.hg8_snapshot_ratio", "statement": "HG-8 wire blobs cut a capture-shaped replica's snapshot to {value} of raw complex64", "value": "0.25x", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/sync.md", "generator": "HoloReplica(codec=...) snapshot bytes; ORStore.compact() against an exact survivor sum"}, "evidence": ["holo/crdt.py", "holo/orset.py", "tests/test_crdt.py"], "patterns": ["84\\.0 MB raw against 21\\.0 MB, ([\\d.]+x)"], "cites": ["docs/sync.md"], "lane": "sync", "notes": "HG-8 wire blobs, measured on a capture-shaped replica. A new dtype code rather than a layout change, so WIRE_VERSION does not move and older builds refuse the blob loudly."}
{"id": "sync.compact_drift_old", "statement": "Subtract-and-repack compaction under HG-8 drifts to {value} over six staged batches", "value": "0.0271", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/sync.md", "generator": "HoloReplica(codec=...) snapshot bytes; ORStore.compact() against an exact survivor sum"}, "evidence": ["holo/crdt.py", "holo/orset.py", "tests/test_crdt.py"], "patterns": ["0\\.0119 rising to ([\\d.]+), 2\\.3x"], "cites": ["docs/sync.md"], "lane": "sync", "notes": "Generation loss in ORStore.compact() under a lossy wire codec: subtracting the doomed items from a decoded blob moves values off the quantisation grid, so each compaction re-quantises an adjusted approximation. Re-encoding survivors from the descriptor index is flat at the codec's one-shot error. Only bites a single epoch compacted repeatedly \u2014 the ORStrokeScene shape."}
{"id": "sync.compact_drift_new", "statement": "Re-encoding survivors from the index holds compaction flat at {value}", "value": "0.0079", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/sync.md", "generator": "HoloReplica(codec=...) snapshot bytes; ORStore.compact() against an exact survivor sum"}, "evidence": ["holo/crdt.py", "holo/orset.py", "tests/test_crdt.py"], "patterns": ["against a flat ([\\d.]+) when the value quantised"], "cites": ["docs/sync.md"], "lane": "sync", "notes": "Generation loss in ORStore.compact() under a lossy wire codec: subtracting the doomed items from a decoded blob moves values off the quantisation grid, so each compaction re-quantises an adjusted approximation. Re-encoding survivors from the descriptor index is flat at the codec's one-shot error. Only bites a single epoch compacted repeatedly \u2014 the ORStrokeScene shape."}
{"id": "sync.compact_rebuild_cost", "statement": "The cold compaction rebuild is {value} the cost of subtracting from the retained exact blob", "value": "158x", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/sync.md", "generator": "ORStore.compact() on a 5,000-item epoch, d=8192, channels=3, hg8"}, "evidence": ["holo/orset.py", "tests/test_orset.py"], "patterns": ["0\\.0097 s on a 5,000-item epoch, ([\\d.]+x)"], "cites": ["docs/sync.md"], "lane": "sync", "notes": "Per-live-item against per-doomed-item, so it is linear in epoch size against constant. Only a cold process pays it: the exact running blob is retained for recent own epochs."}
{"id": "precision.metal_gemm_speedup", "statement": "Applying the per-cell solve operator on Metal in complex64 is {value}x faster than the shipped NumPy float64 path", "value": 6.7, "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-27", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/backend.md", "generator": "python -m bench.precision_battery"}, "evidence": ["bench/precision_battery.py", "tests/test_precision_battery.py"], "patterns": ["float64's 2\\.657 s - ([\\d.]+)x"], "cites": ["docs/backend.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Measured by bench/precision_battery.py on the saguaro capture. The precision question was opened by asking why the projection solve runs on NumPy when encode and decode run on Metal; the first answer given cited a condition number (1.6e20) belonging to a matrix the pipeline never inverts.", "units": "x"}
