{"id": "precision.fp32_factorise_tsvd", "statement": "Computing the TSVD operator itself in float32 costs {value} relative on its action", "value": "1.38e-5", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/backend.md", "generator": "python -m bench.precision_battery --only A2"}, "evidence": ["bench/precision_battery.py", "out/precision/battery.jsonl"], "patterns": ["the same place: ([\\de.-]+) at the shipped truncation"], "cites": ["docs/backend.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Measured by bench/precision_battery.py (A2) on the saguaro capture. Factorising in float32 costs no more than applying in it, so the barrier to moving the whole solve to a low-precision device is MLX's missing GPU linear algebra, not numerics."}
{"id": "project.keep_optimum_saguaro", "statement": "At keep=0.55 the projection reaches {value} on saguaro, against +38.0% at the shipped 0.25", "value": "+59.3%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz --sweep keep=..."}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["0\\.55\\s+(\\+[\\d.]+%)\\s+\\+58\\.8%"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Truncation was chosen for stability, never swept for accuracy. The optimum abuts a cliff: 0.55 is the best setting measured and 0.70 is 37x worse than not projecting. The edge is scene-dependent (lidar-dense's top-down peaks near 0.40), so no fixed default is both safe and good \u2014 which is why the projection stays unpromoted."}
{"id": "project.keep_cliff", "statement": "One truncation step past the optimum the solve is {value} \u2014 worse than not projecting at all", "value": "-1417.0%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz --sweep keep=..."}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["0\\.70\\s+(-[\\d.]+%)\\s+-838\\.2%"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Truncation was chosen for stability, never swept for accuracy. The optimum abuts a cliff: 0.55 is the best setting measured and 0.70 is 37x worse than not projecting. The edge is scene-dependent (lidar-dense's top-down peaks near 0.40), so no fixed default is both safe and good \u2014 which is why the projection stays unpromoted."}
{"id": "project.divergence_norm_gap", "statement": "Working truncations sit at or below a solved/forward norm ratio of {value}, broken ones at or above 97", "value": "5.3", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz --sweep keep=..."}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["0\\.55\\s+\\+59\\.3%\\s+\\+58\\.8%\\s+([\\d.]+)"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Truncation was chosen for stability, never swept for accuracy. The optimum abuts a cliff: 0.55 is the best setting measured and 0.70 is 37x worse than not projecting. The edge is scene-dependent (lidar-dense's top-down peaks near 0.40), so no fixed default is both safe and good \u2014 which is why the projection stays unpromoted."}
{"id": "project.divergence_broken_ratio", "statement": "Every diverged truncation exceeds a solved/forward norm ratio of {value}, against 5.3 for every working one", "value": "97", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "median solved vs forward bundle norm, saguaro xfine, keep sweep"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["everything broken at or above (\\d+), an 18x gap"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "The 18x gap between the last working truncation and the first broken one is what makes DIVERGENCE_RATIO safe to set at 20: it catches every failure and passes the best setting measured."}
{"id": "orset.cell_accumulator_saving", "statement": "Keying epochs by cell holds {value} of accumulator for a 40-cell stroke, against 655.2 MB for a store per cell", "value": "10.0 MB", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/orset.md", "generator": "2621 saguaro cells vs a 40-cell stroke at d=8192, channels=4"}, "evidence": ["holo/orset.py", "tests/test_orset.py"], "patterns": ["four channels is ([\\d.]+ MB) against 655\\.2 MB"], "cites": ["docs/orset.md"], "lane": "sync", "notes": "Cell-keyed epochs at capture scale. A store per cell would hold one (channels, d) accumulator for every cell of the capture; keying by cell holds only the cells the current stroke touched, and keeps a stroke's undo to a single tombstone however many cells it wrote."}
{"id": "project.redrock_fine_share", "statement": "Red Rock's fine band holds {value} of the capture's splats, which is why slice error misses its corruption", "value": "0.7%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "run_projection_pipeline --sweep keep=... on data/iphone/redrock.ply, plus per-cell norm ratios on the fine band"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py"], "patterns": ["The fine band holds ([\\d.]+%) of the splats"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Measured on redrock.ply, the lossless capture docs/real-scenes.md recommends. Corrects an earlier reading taken only on the lossy saguaro .spz: keep=0.55 wins on slice error while destroying the fine band, and the slice metric cannot see it because that band holds 0.7% of the splats. keep=0.25 is the last clean truncation."}
