{"id": "project.redrock_ratio_broken", "statement": "At keep=0.55 every Red Rock fine-band cell exceeds the limit, median norm ratio {value}", "value": "1030", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "run_projection_pipeline --sweep keep=... on data/iphone/redrock.ply, plus per-cell norm ratios on the fine band"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py"], "patterns": ["0\\.55\\s+median (\\d+), p99 2430\\s+100%", "turns \"([\\d]+)x the forward bundle norm\" into a statement"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Measured on redrock.ply, the lossless capture docs/real-scenes.md recommends. Corrects an earlier reading taken only on the lossy saguaro .spz: keep=0.55 wins on slice error while destroying the fine band, and the slice metric cannot see it because that band holds 0.7% of the splats. keep=0.25 is the last clean truncation."}
{"id": "project.keep_fine_cut_d8192", "statement": "At keep=0.55 the fine band's truncation cuts at a relative eigenvalue of {value}, where coarse cuts at 1.79e-03", "value": "2.47e-12", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline --spectrum"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "out/gram_spectrum_d8192.npz"], "patterns": ["At keep=0\\.55 the fine band is cut at ([\\d.e-]+) where", "cuts fine at a relative eigenvalue of ([\\d.e-]+) and coarse"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md", "SDK.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Measured by `run_projection_pipeline.py --spectrum`, which needs no capture: the window Gram depends on (codebook, cell size, window width) alone. `keep` truncates by RANK, which says nothing about how small the smallest surviving eigenvalue is, and the operator divides by it. This is the mechanism behind project.redrock_fine_share - fine is the band a shared rank fraction regularises least, and fine is the band that ran at 1030x on Red Rock. The spread widens with d: a d=2048 rehearsal put this at 4.7e-6, six orders of magnitude short, the same trap docs/fit.md already records for an early per-cell study."}
{"id": "project.keep_band_spread", "statement": "One keep fraction spans a factor of {value} in actual regularisation level between bands at d=8192", "value": "7e8", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline --spectrum"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "out/gram_spectrum_d8192.npz"], "patterns": ["spanning a factor of ([\\de]+) in what it actually regularises", "one nominal setting spanning ([\\de]+) in what it actually", "one setting spans a factor of ([\\de]+) in what it"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md", "SDK.md", "ROADMAP.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Measured by `run_projection_pipeline.py --spectrum`, which needs no capture: the window Gram depends on (codebook, cell size, window width) alone. `keep` truncates by RANK, which says nothing about how small the smallest surviving eigenvalue is, and the operator divides by it. This is the mechanism behind project.redrock_fine_share - fine is the band a shared rank fraction regularises least, and fine is the band that ran at 1030x on Red Rock. The spread widens with d: a d=2048 rehearsal put this at 4.7e-6, six orders of magnitude short, the same trap docs/fit.md already records for an early per-cell study."}
{"id": "project.eps_1e4_fine_fraction", "statement": "A single eps=1e-4 threshold keeps {value} of the fine band's spectrum, against the shipped uniform keep=0.25", "value": "0.195", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline --spectrum"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "out/gram_spectrum_d8192.npz"], "patterns": ["truncates fine harder - ([\\d.]+), and fine is the band"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "The shape a threshold-parameterised truncation would have: it truncates the ill-conditioned `fine` band HARDER than a flat quarter while letting well-conditioned `mid` and `coarse` keep 0.625 and 0.689. NOT a score - no capture has been run at eps yet. Derivable from out/gram_spectrum_d8192.npz without redoing the eigendecompositions."}
{"id": "project.keep_damages_fine", "statement": "At the shipped keep=0.25 the projection decodes Red Rock's fine band {value} WORSE than forward encoding, while the aggregate improves", "value": "24.6% / 33.1%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/iphone/redrock.ply --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["fine decodes ([\\d.]+% / [\\d.]+%) WORSE than not projecting"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md", "SDK.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Found by the per-band referee. 0.0% of cells were over the divergence limit and the norm ratio was 1.32, so both the gate and the aggregate slice error called this setting clean. The aggregate cannot see it because xfine holds 542,122 of 546,638 splats - see project.redrock_fine_share."}
{"id": "project.eps_worst_band", "statement": "eps=1e-3 is the only Red Rock setting measured where no band is meaningfully degraded; its worst is fine at {value}", "value": "-1.0%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/iphone/redrock.ply --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["its worst is fine at (-[\\d.]+%) - and it holds"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "The threshold parameterisation working as designed: it truncates the ill-conditioned fine band hardest (846 of 8192) exactly where a flat rank fraction truncates it least. Costs aggregate to get there - +8.7% against keep=0.25's +17.8% top-down."}
{"id": "project.divergence_limit_slack", "statement": "Every norm ratio in the Red Rock eps sweep is at or below {value}, against a DIVERGENCE_RATIO of 20 \u2014 so the gate passed a setting that degrades a band by a quarter", "value": "4.34", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/iphone/redrock.ply --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["norm ratios in this run are at or below ([\\d.]+), against", "norm ratios are at or below ([\\d.]+) against"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md", "SDK.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "20 was calibrated against catastrophe (saguaro's 5.3-vs-97 gap), which is not the failure that happens at a working setting. Within each sparse band the ratio tracks per-band error monotonically, so a limit near 1.3 would have refused fine at keep=0.25. NOT changed on one capture - the same reasoning that made 20 wrong would make 1.3 wrong."}
{"id": "project.keep_damages_fine_saguaro", "statement": "keep=0.25 degrades saguaro's fine band by {value}, confirming the Red Rock defect transfers", "value": "-29.4% / -34.8%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["damages fine again - (-[\\d.]+% / -[\\d.]+%) here against", "damages fine again \\((-[\\d.]+% / -[\\d.]+%) against"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md", "SDK.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Red Rock gave -24.6% / -33.1% at the same setting (project.keep_damages_fine). Same direction, same order of magnitude, two captures - so the shipped setting's band regression is a property of the technique, not of one scene."}
{"id": "project.eps_beats_keep_saguaro", "statement": "On saguaro eps=1e-4 beats the shipped keep=0.25 on the aggregate too, at {value}", "value": "+42.6% / +40.6%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["eps=1e-4\\s+(\\+[\\d.]+% / \\+[\\d.]+%)\\s+\\+42\\.7%", "on the aggregate TOO \\((\\+[\\d.]+% / \\+[\\d.]+%) against"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md", "SDK.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Against keep=0.25's +38.0% / +35.9%, while leaving fine at -1.9% / -5.3% instead of -29.4% / -34.8%. On Red Rock the aggregate went the other way (-4.3 / -3.0 points), so across both captures eps=1e-4 is a wash on aggregate and ~25 points better on fine. NOT shipped: lidar-dense is untested and is the capture that already disagreed about keep."}
{"id": "project.faint_band_artifact", "statement": "Saguaro's coarse band reported a relative error of {value} before a signal floor existed \u2014 a division by nearly nothing, not a failure", "value": "4,359,160", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-28", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/scan-tucson.spz --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["run reported\\s+\\*?\\*?([\\d,]+)\\*?\\*? for it", "reported a relative error of ([\\d,]+)\\."], "cites": ["docs/fit.md", "SDK.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "rel_err guarded only an EXACTLY zero referee; a band with a few distant splats gives a nearly zero one. SIGNAL_FLOOR now declines to score a band holding under a thousandth of the field at the probe points. Found by reading a real run's output rather than by a test."}
{"id": "project.lidar_dense_single_band", "statement": "lidar-dense populates exactly one band ({value} cells of `mid`), so it cannot test a finding about minority bands", "value": 241, "units": "cells", "kind": "count", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-29", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/iphone/lidar-dense.ply --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["one band, mid, with ([\\d,]+) cells"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Its aggregate IS that band by construction. Chosen as the third capture because it had already disagreed with the other two about keep; it turns out to be structurally silent on the band question and contributes only four points in the safe regime (ratios 0.98 to 1.07, all improvements)."}
{"id": "project.redrock_coarse_unreconstructed", "statement": "Red Rock's coarse band has a forward error of {value} \u2014 above 1.0, so the pipeline reconstructs it worse than returning zeros", "value": "1.4294", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-08-29", "version": "0.3.0"}, "source": {"doc": "docs/fit.md", "generator": "python -m examples.run_projection_pipeline data/iphone/lidar-dense.ply --sweep keep=0.25 --sweep eps=1e-3,1e-4,1e-5 --allow-divergence"}, "evidence": ["examples/run_projection_pipeline.py", "tests/test_projection_gram.py"], "patterns": ["FORWARD error of ([\\d.]+) - above 1\\.0"], "cites": ["docs/fit.md"], "lane": "research", "notes": "Matters because that band's norm ratio would otherwise veto a run: a band that never worked cannot be damaged. Same class of error as the one SIGNAL_FLOOR fixes for the error metric, in the divergence metric instead. 21 splats of 546,638."}
{"id": "capture.err_brookline", "statement": "The Brookline springhouse interior decodes at {value} slice error vs exact ground truth", "value": "15.9%/28.2%", "kind": "measurement", "status": "current", "as_of": {"date": "2026-09-04", "version": "0.3.0"}, "evidence": ["results/real_brookline-station.png"], "patterns": ["\\b(15\\.9%/28\\.2%)"], "cites": ["docs/real-scenes.md"], "lane": "capture", "notes": "Run 20260904T073902 (out/runs/2026-09-04.jsonl, 1423 s, 8.25 GB peak). Input: Scaniverse raw 3DGS .ply of a stone interior, 563,482 splats after the gallery crop (data/brookline-station.ply, gitignored like all captures). Deterministic encode - single run is the measurement. Best single-axis slice number of any real capture; the 28.2% side axis reflects an interior scanned from within (one axis never crossed by the camera)."}
